      {
        num: '01',
        heading: 'I design the architecture.',
        body: 'Event-driven on AWS, built to survive real load: 1,000+ concurrent connections and thousands of requests a second at 99.9% uptime. The diagram on this page is the shape of a real production system — request in, retrieval and reasoning across vector and graph stores, model calls fanned out across OpenAI, Bedrock, Azure and Mistral.',
      },
      {
        num: '02',
        heading: 'I build the pipelines and evals.',
        body: 'RAG that earns trust: chunking and retrieval you can defend, evals that catch regressions before your users do, and audit trails wired in from day one. I took my company through ISO 27001 and SOC 2 in ~3 months — because in regulated markets, compliance is part of the architecture, not an afterthought.',
      },
      {
        num: '03',
        heading: 'I lead the engineers who own it.',
        body: "I've built a company from 0 to €1M+ revenue and a team from 0 to 10. At idealo, multi-country SSO I led drove 1.4M new accounts in three months — +700% versus forecast. I hand systems over to teams that keep shipping after I've moved on.",
      },
    ],
    ctaTitle: "Send me your pipeline. I'll tell you where it breaks.",
    ctaSub:
      "A short, specific read of your RAG or event-driven setup — retrieval, evals, scaling, and the compliance gaps you'll hit in a regulated market. No slides, no proof-of-concept theatre.",
