    heroSub:
      "Multi-tenant RAG na event-driven AWS — ponad 1000 jednoczesnych połączeń, tysiące requestów na sekundę, 99,9% uptime, dla ponad 50 organizacji z branż regulowanych. Projektuję architekturę, buduję pipeline'y i evale, podpinam audit traile i prowadzę inżynierów, którzy potem to utrzymują. <strong>Nie kolejne proof-of-concept.</strong>",
    ctaPrimary: 'Przejdź przez architekturę',
    ctaGhost: 'Podeślij mi swój pipeline — powiem Ci, gdzie się posypie',
    availability: 'Obecnie doradzam · otwarty na właściwą stałą rolę CTO',
    diagramTitle: 'System live',
    diagramHealth: '99,9% uptime',
    throughputLabel: 'przepustowość na żywo',
    svgAriaLabel:
      'Diagram architektury: Client do API Gateway do Lambda i Fargate do RAG Service do baz Vector i Graph oraz dostawców LLM OpenAI, Bedrock, Azure i Mistral.',
    proofKicker: 'Systemy wdrożone dla',
    stats: [
      { value: '1,000+', label: 'jednoczesnych połączeń' },
      { value: 'thousands', label: 'requestów / sekundę' },
      { value: '99.9%', label: 'uptime' },
      { value: '50+', label: 'organizacji regulowanych' },
    ],
    details: [
      {
        num: '01',
        heading: 'Projektuję architekturę.',
        body: 'Event-driven na AWS, zbudowane tak, by wytrzymać prawdziwe obciążenie: ponad 1000 jednoczesnych połączeń i tysiące requestów na sekundę przy 99,9% uptime. Diagram na tej stronie to kształt realnego systemu produkcyjnego — request wchodzi, retrieval i reasoning w bazach wektorowych i grafowych, wywołania modeli rozłożone między OpenAI, Bedrock, Azure i Mistral.',
      },
      {
        num: '02',
        heading: "Buduję pipeline'y i evale.",
        body: 'RAG, który zasługuje na zaufanie: chunking i retrieval, których obronisz przed każdym, evale wyłapujące regresje, zanim zrobią to Twoi użytkownicy, i audit traile podpięte od pierwszego dnia. Przeprowadziłem swoją firmę przez ISO 27001 i SOC 2 w około 3 miesiące — bo na rynkach regulowanych compliance to część architektury, a nie coś doklejanego na końcu.',
      },
      {
        num: '03',
        heading: 'Prowadzę inżynierów, którzy potem to utrzymują.',
        body: 'Zbudowałem firmę od zera do ponad 1 mln € przychodu i zespół od zera do 10 osób. W idealo prowadziłem wielokrajowe SSO, które w trzy miesiące dało 1,4 mln nowych kont — +700% względem prognozy. Przekazuję systemy zespołom, które dalej dowożą, kiedy mnie już nie ma.',
      },
    ],
    ctaTitle: 'Podeślij mi swój pipeline. Powiem Ci, gdzie się posypie.',
    ctaSub:
      'Krótka, konkretna analiza Twojego setupu RAG albo event-driven — retrieval, evale, skalowanie i luki w compliance, na które trafisz na rynku regulowanym. Bez slajdów, bez teatru z proof-of-concept.',
    ctaActionPrimary: 'Podeślij mi swój pipeline',
    ctaActionGhost: 'Przejdź przez architekturę jeszcze raz',
  },
  de: {
    metaTitle: 'Jacek Janczura — AI Systems Architect & Fractional CTO',
    metaDescription:
      'Das Multi-tenant-RAG-System, das du gerade bauen willst, habe ich schon in Produktion gebracht. Event-driven auf AWS, über 1.000 gleichzeitige Verbindungen, Tausende Requests pro Sekunde, 99,9% Uptime, für über 50 regulierte Organisationen.',
    eyebrow: 'AI Systems Architect · Fractional CTO',
    heroTitle:
      'Das AI-System, das du bauen willst,<br class="br-desktop" /> läuft bei mir schon.',
    heroSub:
      'Multi-tenant RAG auf event-driven AWS — über 1.000 gleichzeitige Verbindungen, Tausende Requests pro Sekunde, 99,9% Uptime, für über 50 regulierte Organisationen. Ich entwerfe die Architektur, baue die Pipelines und Evals, verdrahte die Audit-Trails und führe die Engineers, die das Ganze am Ende besitzen. <strong>Kein weiteres Proof-of-Concept.</strong>',
    ctaPrimary: 'Geh mit mir durch die Architektur',
    ctaGhost: 'Schick mir deine Pipeline — ich sag dir, wo sie bricht',
    availability:
      'Aktuell als Berater tätig · offen für die richtige feste CTO-Rolle',
    diagramTitle: 'Live-System',
    diagramHealth: '99,9% Uptime',
    throughputLabel: 'Live-Durchsatz',
    svgAriaLabel:
      'Architekturdiagramm: Client zu API Gateway zu Lambda und Fargate zu RAG Service zu Vector- und Graph-Datenbanken sowie den LLM-Providern OpenAI, Bedrock, Azure und Mistral.',
    proofKicker: 'Systeme ausgeliefert für',
    stats: [
      { value: '1,000+', label: 'gleichzeitige Verbindungen' },
      { value: 'thousands', label: 'Requests / Sekunde' },
      { value: '99.9%', label: 'Uptime' },
      { value: '50+', label: 'regulierte Organisationen' },
    ],
    details: [
      {
        num: '01',
        heading: 'Ich entwerfe die Architektur.',
        body: 'Event-driven auf AWS, gebaut, um echte Last auszuhalten: über 1.000 gleichzeitige Verbindungen und Tausende Requests pro Sekunde bei 99,9% Uptime. Das Diagramm auf dieser Seite ist die Form eines echten Produktionssystems — Request rein, Retrieval und Reasoning über Vector- und Graph-Stores, Modell-Calls verteilt über OpenAI, Bedrock, Azure und Mistral.',
      },
      {
        num: '02',
        heading: 'Ich baue die Pipelines und Evals.',
        body: 'RAG, das Vertrauen verdient: Chunking und Retrieval, die du verteidigen kannst, Evals, die Regressionen abfangen, bevor deine Nutzer sie merken, und Audit-Trails, von Tag eins an verdrahtet. Ich habe meine Firma in rund 3 Monaten durch ISO 27001 und SOC 2 gebracht — denn in regulierten Märkten ist Compliance Teil der Architektur, kein nachträglicher Gedanke.',
      },
      {
        num: '03',
        heading: 'Ich führe die Engineers, die das System besitzen.',
        body: 'Ich habe eine Firma von 0 auf über 1 Mio. € Umsatz und ein Team von 0 auf 10 aufgebaut. Bei idealo trieb das länderübergreifende SSO, das ich verantwortet habe, in drei Monaten 1,4 Mio. neue Accounts — +700% gegenüber Forecast. Ich übergebe Systeme an Teams, die weiter ausliefern, wenn ich längst weiter bin.',
      },
    ],
    ctaTitle: 'Schick mir deine Pipeline. Ich sag dir, wo sie bricht.',
    ctaSub:
      'Ein kurzer, konkreter Blick auf dein RAG- oder event-driven Setup — Retrieval, Evals, Skalierung und die Compliance-Lücken, auf die du in einem regulierten Markt triffst. Keine Slides, kein Proof-of-Concept-Theater.',
    ctaActionPrimary: 'Schick mir deine Pipeline',
    ctaActionGhost: 'Nochmal durch die Architektur',
  },
};

const t = copy[lang];
const stats = t.stats;
---

<BaseLayout title={t.metaTitle} description={t.metaDescription} lang={lang}>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero__grid">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow reveal">{t.eyebrow}</p>
        <h1
          class="hero__title reveal"
          style="--reveal-delay: 60ms"
          set:html={t.heroTitle}
        />
        <p
          class="hero__sub reveal"
          style="--reveal-delay: 120ms"
          set:html={t.heroSub}
        />
        <div class="hero__cta reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 180ms">
          <a href="#architecture" class="btn btn--primary">
            {t.ctaPrimary}
          </a>
          <a href="#pipeline" class="btn btn--ghost">
            {t.ctaGhost}
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="availability reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 240ms">
          <span class="availability__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          {t.availability}
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Signature animation: self-drawing architecture diagram -->
      <div class="hero__diagram reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 120ms">
        <div class="diagram-card" id="diagram-card">
          <div class="diagram-card__head">
            <span class="diagram-card__title">{t.diagramTitle}</span>
            <span class="diagram-card__health" id="health-readout">
              <span class="diagram-card__pulse" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              {t.diagramHealth}
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="diagram-stage">
            <svg
              class="arch"
              id="arch-svg"
              viewBox="0 0 480 420"
              role="img"
              aria-label={t.svgAriaLabel}
              preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"
            >
              <defs>
                <linearGradient id="edgeGrad" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">
                  <stop offset="0" stop-color="var(--primary)"></stop>
                  <stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--accent)"></stop>
                </linearGradient>
              </defs>

              <!-- Edges (drawn first, behind nodes) -->
              <g
                class="edges"
                fill="none"
                stroke="url(#edgeGrad)"
                stroke-width="2"
              >
                <path class="edge" data-from="0" d="M90 48 H240 V96"></path>
                <path class="edge" data-from="1" d="M240 132 V150 H150 V174"
                ></path>
                <path class="edge" data-from="1" d="M240 132 V150 H330 V174"
                ></path>
                <path class="edge" data-from="2" d="M150 210 V228 H240 V252"
                ></path>
                <path class="edge" data-from="2" d="M330 210 V228 H240 V252"
                ></path>
                <path class="edge" data-from="3" d="M240 288 V306 H120 V330"
                ></path>
                <path class="edge" data-from="3" d="M240 288 V306 H360 V330"
                ></path>
                <path class="edge" data-from="4" d="M240 288 V372"></path>
              </g>

              <!-- Data-flow pulse dots (positioned by JS along edges) -->
              <g class="pulses" fill="var(--accent)"></g>

              <!-- Nodes. Position lives on the outer <g> (transform attribute);
                   the inner .node-fx carries the CSS entrance transform so the
                   two never collide. -->
              <g class="nodes" font-family="var(--font-heading)">
                <g class="node" data-step="0" transform="translate(30 30)">
                  <g class="node-fx">
                    <rect width="120" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                    <text x="60" y="23">Client</text>
                  </g>
                </g>
                <g
                  class="node node--gw"
                  data-step="1"
                  transform="translate(170 96)"
                >
                  <g class="node-fx">
                    <rect width="140" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                    <text x="70" y="23">API Gateway</text>
                  </g>
                </g>
                <g class="node" data-step="2" transform="translate(90 174)">
                  <g class="node-fx">
                    <rect width="120" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                    <text x="60" y="23">Lambda</text>
                  </g>
                </g>
                <g class="node" data-step="2" transform="translate(270 174)">
                  <g class="node-fx">
                    <rect width="120" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                    <text x="60" y="23">Fargate</text>
                  </g>
                </g>
                <g
                  class="node node--core"
                  data-step="3"
                  transform="translate(160 252)"
                >
                  <g class="node-fx">
                    <rect width="160" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                    <text x="80" y="23">RAG Service</text>
                  </g>
                </g>
                <g class="node" data-step="4" transform="translate(50 330)">
                  <g class="node-fx">
                    <rect width="140" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                    <text x="70" y="23">Vector DB</text>
                  </g>
                </g>
                <g class="node" data-step="4" transform="translate(290 330)">
                  <g class="node-fx">
                    <rect width="140" height="36" rx="9"></rect>
                    <text x="70" y="23">Graph DB</text>
                  </g>
                </g>
                <g
                  class="node node--llm"
                  data-step="4"
                  transform="translate(140 384)"
                >
                  <g class="node-fx">
                    <rect width="200" height="28" rx="9"></rect>
                    <text x="100" y="19"
                      >OpenAI · Bedrock · Azure · Mistral</text
                    >
                  </g>
                </g>
              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <div class="diagram-card__foot">
            <div class="throughput">
              <span class="throughput__value" id="throughput">~0 req/sec</span>
              <span class="throughput__label">{t.throughputLabel}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="meter" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="meter__fill" id="meter-fill"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Proof wall: named clients -->
  <section class="proof" id="proof">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="proof__kicker reveal">{t.proofKicker}</p>
      <ul class="logo-wall reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 60ms">
        {
          logos.map((logo, i) => (
            <li class="logo-chip" style={`--chip-delay: ${i * 55}ms`}>
              <img
                src={logo.src}
                alt={logo.alt}
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>

      <dl class="stat-row reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 120ms">
        {
          stats.map(s => (
            <div class="stat">
              <dt class="stat__value">{s.value}</dt>
              <dd class="stat__label">{s.label}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Architecture walk-through anchor -->
  <section class="detail" id="architecture">
    <div class="container detail__grid">
      <article class="detail__col reveal">
        <span class="detail__num">{t.details[0].num}</span>
        <h2>{t.details[0].heading}</h2>
        <p>
          {t.details[0].body}
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail__col reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 80ms">
        <span class="detail__num">{t.details[1].num}</span>
        <h2>{t.details[1].heading}</h2>
        <p>
          {t.details[1].body}
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail__col reveal" style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        <span class="detail__num">{t.details[2].num}</span>
        <h2>{t.details[2].heading}</h2>
        <p>
          {t.details[2].body}
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Pipeline CTA anchor -->
  <section class="cta" id="pipeline">
    <div class="container cta__inner reveal">
      <h2 class="cta__title">
        {t.ctaTitle}
      </h2>
      <p class="cta__sub">
        {t.ctaSub}
      </p>
      <div class="cta__actions">
        <a
          href="mailto:hello@janczura.com?subject=Pipeline%20review"
          class="btn btn--primary"
        >
          {t.ctaActionPrimary}
        </a>
        <a href="#architecture" class="btn btn--ghost">{t.ctaActionGhost}</a>
      </div>
      <p class="availability availability--foot">
        <span class="availability__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {t.availability}
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* ---------- Hero ---------- */
  .hero {
    padding: var(--space-9) 0 var(--space-8);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .hero__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(0, 0.95fr);
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--primary);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }

  .hero__title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6.4vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.06;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  }

  .hero__sub {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.4vw, 1.15rem);
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }
  .hero__sub strong {
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .hero__cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-3) var(--space-5);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    line-height: 1.2;
    text-align: center;
    text-decoration: none;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      transform 0.22s var(--ease-out),
      box-shadow 0.22s var(--ease-out),
      background-color 0.22s var(--ease-out),
      border-color 0.22s var(--ease-out);
  }
  .btn:hover {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .btn--primary {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: #fff;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-2);
  }
  .btn--ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--text);
    border-color: var(--border);
  }
  .btn:active {
    transform: scale(0.97);
  }
  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .btn--primary:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-3);
    }
    .btn--ghost:hover {
      border-color: var(--primary);
      color: var(--primary);
    }
  }

  /* Availability pill */
  .availability {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--muted-fg, var(--text));
    opacity: 0.85;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .availability__dot {
    width: 8px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 var(--accent);
    animation: availPulse 2.6s var(--ease-out) infinite;
    flex: none;
  }
  @keyframes availPulse {
    0% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 color-mix(in oklch, var(--accent) 55%, transparent);
    }
    70% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 7px color-mix(in oklch, var(--accent) 0%, transparent);
    }
    100% {
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 color-mix(in oklch, var(--accent) 0%, transparent);
    }
  }

  /* ---------- Diagram card ---------- */
  .hero__diagram {
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .diagram-card {
    background: var(--bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-3);
    padding: var(--space-4);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  /* faint grid texture so it reads as an "instrument", not a box */
  .diagram-card::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(
        color-mix(in oklch, var(--border) 45%, transparent) 1px,
        transparent 1px
      ),
      linear-gradient(
        90deg,
        color-mix(in oklch, var(--border) 45%, transparent) 1px,
        transparent 1px
      );
    background-size: 26px 26px;
    opacity: 0.35;
    pointer-events: none;
    mask-image: radial-gradient(120% 90% at 50% 0%, #000 40%, transparent 100%);
  }
  .diagram-card > * {
    position: relative;
  }

  .diagram-card__head,
  .diagram-card__foot {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .diagram-card__head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .diagram-card__title {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text);
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .diagram-card__health {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .diagram-card__pulse {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    animation: availPulse 2.6s var(--ease-out) infinite;
  }

  .diagram-stage {
    width: 100%;
  }
  .arch {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Nodes */
  .arch .node rect {
    fill: var(--bg);
    stroke: var(--border);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08));
  }
  .arch .node--gw rect,
  .arch .node--core rect {
    stroke: var(--primary);
  }
  .arch .node--core rect {
    fill: color-mix(in oklch, var(--primary) 10%, var(--bg));
  }
  .arch .node--llm rect {
    fill: color-mix(in oklch, var(--accent) 12%, var(--bg));
    stroke: var(--accent);
  }
  .arch .node text {
    fill: var(--text);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-anchor: middle;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
  }
  .arch .node--llm text {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  }

  /* Foot: throughput + meter */
  .diagram-card__foot {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .throughput {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    line-height: 1.15;
  }
  .throughput__value {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    color: var(--primary);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .throughput__label {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
  .meter {
    flex: 1;
    max-width: 160px;
    height: 8px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--muted);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .meter__fill {
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    width: 8%;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--primary), var(--accent));
    transition: width 0.4s var(--ease-out);
  }

  /* ---------- Proof wall ---------- */
  .proof {
    padding: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-8);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .proof__kicker {
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    opacity: 0.6;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5);
  }
  .logo-wall {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-7);
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .logo-wall {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(7, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .logo-chip {
    background: #fff;
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.05);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: var(--space-4);
    min-height: 68px;
    transition:
      transform 0.28s var(--ease-out),
      box-shadow 0.28s var(--ease-out);
  }
  .reveal-on .logo-chip {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(14px);
  }
  .reveal-on .logo-wall.is-visible .logo-chip {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: none;
    transition:
      opacity 0.55s var(--ease-out) var(--chip-delay, 0ms),
      transform 0.55s var(--ease-out) var(--chip-delay, 0ms);
  }
  .logo-chip img {
    max-width: 100%;
    max-height: 34px;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
  }
  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .logo-chip:hover {
      transform: translateY(-3px);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow-2);
    }
  }

  /* Stat row */
  .stat-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (min-width: 560px) {
    .stat-row {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }
  .stat {
    text-align: center;
    padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-2);
    border-radius: var(--radius-m);
    background: var(--muted);
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }
  .stat__value {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3.5vw, 1.7rem);
    color: var(--primary);
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.1;
  }
  .stat__label {
    margin: var(--space-1) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    opacity: 0.72;
  }

  /* ---------- Detail columns ---------- */
  .detail {
    padding: var(--space-8) 0;
  }
  .detail__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }
  .detail__num {
    font-family: var(--font-heading);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  }
  .detail__col h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.6vw, 1.7rem);
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-3);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .detail__col p {
    margin: 0;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }

  /* ---------- CTA ---------- */
  .cta {
    padding: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-9);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .cta__inner {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 720px;
  }
  .cta__title {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .cta__sub {
    opacity: 0.82;
    margin: 0 auto var(--space-5);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }
  .cta__actions {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }
  .availability--foot {
    justify-content: center;
  }

  /* ---------- Responsive ---------- */
  .br-desktop {
    display: none;
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .br-desktop {
      display: inline;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .hero__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: var(--space-7);
    }
    .hero {
      padding-top: var(--space-8);
    }
    .diagram-card {
      max-width: 460px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
  }

  /* ---------- Reduced motion: static, everything visible ---------- */
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .availability__dot,
    .diagram-card__pulse {
      animation: none;
    }
    .reveal-on .logo-chip {
      opacity: 1 !important;
      transform: none !important;
    }
    .meter__fill {
      transition: none;
    }
    .btn {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>

<script is:inline>
  (function () {
    const svg = document.getElementById('arch-svg');
    const card = document.getElementById('diagram-card');
    const throughputEl = document.getElementById('throughput');
    const meterFill = document.getElementById('meter-fill');
    if (!svg || !card) return;

    const reduce =
      window.matchMedia &&
      window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

    const edges = Array.prototype.slice.call(svg.querySelectorAll('.edge'));
    const nodes = Array.prototype.slice.call(svg.querySelectorAll('.node'));
    const pulseGroup = svg.querySelector('.pulses');

    // ---- Static fallback for reduced motion: draw everything, final numbers ----
    if (reduce) {
      edges.forEach(function (e) {
        e.style.strokeDasharray = 'none';
        e.style.strokeDashoffset = '0';
        e.style.opacity = '1';
      });
      nodes.forEach(function (n) {
        const fx = n.querySelector('.node-fx');
        if (fx) fx.style.opacity = '1';
      });
      if (throughputEl) throughputEl.textContent = '~3,200 req/sec';
      if (meterFill) meterFill.style.width = '80%';
      return;
    }

    // ---- Prime nodes + edges hidden, ready to reveal ----
    nodes.forEach(function (n) {
      const fx = n.querySelector('.node-fx');
      if (!fx) return;
      fx.style.opacity = '0';
      fx.style.transformBox = 'fill-box';
      fx.style.transformOrigin = 'center';
      fx.style.transform = 'translateY(8px) scale(0.96)';
      fx.style.transition =
        'opacity 0.5s var(--ease-out), transform 0.5s var(--ease-out)';
    });

    edges.forEach(function (e) {
      const len = e.getTotalLength ? e.getTotalLength() : 300;
      e.style.strokeDasharray = len;
      e.style.strokeDashoffset = len;
      e.style.opacity = '0.9';
      e.style.transition = 'stroke-dashoffset 0.6s var(--ease-out)';
    });

    // ---- Data-flow pulse dots (rAF along edges) ----
    const dots = edges.map(function (edge) {
      const c = document.createElementNS(
        'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg',
        'circle',
      );
      c.setAttribute('r', '3');
      c.setAttribute('fill', 'var(--accent)');
      c.style.opacity = '0';
      if (pulseGroup) pulseGroup.appendChild(c);
      return {
        el: c,
        edge: edge,
        len: edge.getTotalLength ? edge.getTotalLength() : 300,
        // staggered start + varied speed so flow feels organic
        t: Math.random(),
        speed: 0.28 + Math.random() * 0.22,
      };
    });

    let running = false;
    let rafId = null;
    let last = 0;

    function tickDots(now) {
      if (!running) return;
      const dt = last ? Math.min((now - last) / 1000, 0.05) : 0.016;
      last = now;
      for (let i = 0; i < dots.length; i++) {
        const d = dots[i];
        d.t += d.speed * dt;
        if (d.t > 1) d.t -= 1;
        const p = d.edge.getPointAtLength(d.t * d.len);
        d.el.setAttribute('cx', p.x);
        d.el.setAttribute('cy', p.y);
        // fade at ends so dots don't pop
        const edgeFade = Math.min(d.t, 1 - d.t) * 6;
        d.el.style.opacity = String(Math.min(0.9, edgeFade));
      }
      rafId = window.requestAnimationFrame(tickDots);
    }

    function startDots() {
      if (running) return;
      running = true;
      last = 0;
      rafId = window.requestAnimationFrame(tickDots);
    }
    function stopDots() {
      running = false;
      if (rafId) window.cancelAnimationFrame(rafId);
      rafId = null;
    }

    // ---- Throughput + uptime counters (interval, cheap) ----
    let counterTimer = null;
    let displayed = 0;
    const target = 3200;

    function fmt(n) {
      return '~' + Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US') + ' req/sec';
    }

    function startCounters() {
      // ramp up to target, then breathe subtly around it
      let phase = 'ramp';
      let breatheT = 0;
      counterTimer = window.setInterval(function () {
        if (phase === 'ramp') {
          displayed += (target - displayed) * 0.14 + 4;
          if (displayed >= target - 12) {
            displayed = target;
            phase = 'breathe';
          }
        } else {
          breatheT += 0.18;
          // gentle +/- 220 wander, never shouty
          displayed =
            target + Math.sin(breatheT) * 180 + Math.sin(breatheT * 2.3) * 40;
        }
        if (throughputEl) throughputEl.textContent = fmt(displayed);
        if (meterFill) {
          const pct = 12 + (Math.min(displayed, 4000) / 4000) * 76;
          meterFill.style.width = pct.toFixed(1) + '%';
        }
      }, 90);
    }
    function stopCounters() {
      if (counterTimer) window.clearInterval(counterTimer);
      counterTimer = null;
    }

    // ---- Orchestrated reveal: edges draw, nodes pop, staggered ----
    let played = false;
    function play() {
      if (played) return;
      played = true;

      // group nodes by step for staggered entrance
      const steps = {};
      nodes.forEach(function (n) {
        const s = n.getAttribute('data-step') || '0';
        (steps[s] = steps[s] || []).push(n);
      });

      const stepKeys = Object.keys(steps).sort();
      const base = 120;
      stepKeys.forEach(function (key, idx) {
        const group = steps[key];
        window.setTimeout(
          function () {
            group.forEach(function (n, j) {
              window.setTimeout(function () {
                const fx = n.querySelector('.node-fx');
                if (fx) {
                  fx.style.opacity = '1';
                  fx.style.transform = 'none';
                }
              }, j * 60);
            });
            // draw the edges leaving this step after its nodes appear
            window.setTimeout(function () {
              edges
                .filter(function (e) {
                  return e.getAttribute('data-from') === key;
                })
                .forEach(function (e, k) {
                  window.setTimeout(function () {
                    e.style.strokeDashoffset = '0';
                  }, k * 70);
                });
            }, 180);
          },
          base + idx * 260,
        );
      });

      // once the flow is drawn, bring it alive
      window.setTimeout(
        function () {
          startDots();
          startCounters();
        },
        base + stepKeys.length * 260 + 300,
      );
    }

    // ---- Pause work when the card is off-screen (perf) ----
    const io =
      'IntersectionObserver' in window
        ? new IntersectionObserver(
            function (entries) {
              entries.forEach(function (entry) {
                if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                  play();
                  if (played && !running) startDots();
                  if (played && !counterTimer) startCounters();
                } else {
                  stopDots();
                  stopCounters();
                }
              });
            },
            { threshold: 0.25 },
          )
        : null;

    if (io) {
      io.observe(card);
    } else {
      play();
    }

    // stop loops when tab hidden
    document.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () {
      if (document.hidden) {
        stopDots();
        stopCounters();
      } else if (played) {
        startDots();
        startCounters();
      }
    });
  })();
</script>
